  "id": "DrugBank_DB11186 - MONDO_grouped_11786_5324_24332",
  "verbalization": "Pentoxyverine is implicated in the pathogenesis of Allergic Rhinitis through a series of indirect pathways, all of which involve Vasomotor Rhinitis. The drug is linked to Vasomotor Rhinitis via its indication, and this condition is further connected to Allergic Rhinitis through the indications of its downstream agents, Mizolastine and Ramatroban. These agents are known to target histamine receptors and modulate inflammatory responses, which are central to allergic rhinitis. The shared pathway from Pentoxyverine to Vasomotor Rhinitis suggests a potential mechanism of action that may involve similar pharmacological targets or pathways. The evidence supports a possible role for Pentoxyverine in the treatment or modulation of allergic rhinitis through its interaction with vasomotor pathways, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
